WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.269
-Our next guest is a former
United States Congressman

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:06.272
and currently the Democratic
nominee for governor of Texas.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.808
Please welcome back to the show
Beto O'Rourke, everyone.

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.543
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:16.082 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:21.621 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:23.022
Welcome back!

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:25.091
It's always lovely to have you
back in New York City.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:27.960
We talked last time about how
you spent some time in Brooklyn.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.063
You had Busta Rhymes' -- an old
trampoline from Busta Rhymes

00:00:31.063 --> 00:00:33.199
on the roof of your apartment,
which is a pretty cool thing.

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:34.634
-Very cool thing.
-Yeah.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.068
-A big memory.

00:00:36.068 --> 00:00:37.337
-Yeah.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:38.804
-You also drove --
One of your jobs when you were

00:00:38.804 --> 00:00:42.175
living in Brooklyn is you
drove around famous artwork?

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:45.178
-I worked for a company called
Hedley's Humpers.

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:46.446
-Okay.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:47.680
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.483
-And we would receive
and crate pieces of art

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:52.418
that were bought
by our customers,

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:54.820
and then deliver them
to their homes.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:57.891
And so, yeah, I would be driving
down the streets of New York

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:00.860
in a box truck
with amazing pieces of art.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.496
One time I was able
to handle a Picasso...

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.264
-Wow.
-...if you can believe this.

00:01:05.264 --> 00:01:08.568
You know, what am I,
23 years old, and I've got

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.837
a Picasso in my hands
delivering for a client.

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:12.805
-I was going to say,
it's a terrible --

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:14.574
Hedley Humpers
is a terrible name,

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.776
except I don't think
anyone would ever think

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.944
a Picasso would be in a truck...
-Right.

00:01:18.944 --> 00:01:21.080
-Like, you would be like,
"Well, that's probably just full

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.581
of old pillows or something."

00:01:22.581 --> 00:01:23.750
-Right, right, right.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.952
But amazing people
who worked there.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.753
Most of them were artists.
I was not.

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:31.357
One guy -- went on to have a
great career -- named Dave Ford,

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:33.993
who does these amazing
interactive sculptures,

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:37.096
including one that he developed
by putting canvas

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:39.132
down on the floor of the truck

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:42.101
and then hanging drawing
implements from the ceiling,

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:44.704
and it would record
this kind of kinetic map

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.672
of our journeys along the way.

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:48.341
And, you know, now you
can't get your hands on them

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.442
because they're so valuable.

00:01:50.442 --> 00:01:52.578
But amazing experience.
Loved living in New York.

00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:55.248
But soon enough, I knew
I needed to be back in Texas.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:57.216
-Yes.
-Because that's where I'm from.

00:01:57.216 --> 00:01:58.417
My family's there.

00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:01.921
And I just missed the state,
missed home.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.322
-So, back in Texas,

00:02:03.322 --> 00:02:05.491
you're running against
Governor Greg Abbott.

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:08.695
And obviously, you know,
Texas --

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:11.030
He, you know, banned abortion
after six weeks.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:14.100
And that, I think,
is scary enough,

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.403
but he also implemented
this bounty law.

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.973
Can you explain
exactly how harrowing

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:22.308
this element of his law is?

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:25.778
-Yeah, so, there's
a law in force right now

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:27.913
that is a six-week abortion ban

00:02:27.913 --> 00:02:31.550
with a $10,000 bounty placed
on the back of anyone

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:32.785
who assists any woman

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.254
in making her own decision
about her own life,

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:37.256
her own body,
her own health care.

00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:39.124
But it's actually worse because

00:02:39.124 --> 00:02:41.594
he also signed what is known
as a trigger bill,

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:45.565
which means that if the Supreme
Court overturns Roe v. Wade,

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:49.301
which is likely to happen,
it triggers a total abortion ban

00:02:49.301 --> 00:02:51.070
beginning at conception,

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:55.308
with no exception for rape
and no exception for incest.

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:57.409
And that's happening
in a state that leads

00:02:57.409 --> 00:03:00.813
much of the developed world in
a crisis of maternal mortality.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:02.915
It means that our moms and women

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:05.384
are dying faster
than almost anywhere else

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:06.986
because as you close down

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.755
all these reproductive
health-care clinics,

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.656
not only is it harder
to get an abortion,

00:03:10.656 --> 00:03:12.725
it's harder to get
a cervical cancer screening

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:14.426
or to see a family
planning provider

00:03:14.426 --> 00:03:16.329
or to get a doctor at all

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:18.297
in the least-insured state
in the country.

00:03:18.297 --> 00:03:20.833
So this is deeply,
deeply harmful,

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.603
and, frankly, deadly
to the women of Texas.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:26.839
That's why we've got to win
this race, win political power,

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.807
and get the state
back on the right track

00:03:28.807 --> 00:03:31.644
so every woman can make her
own decision about her own body,

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.379
her own future,
and her own health care.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:35.214
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:35.214 --> 00:03:38.183
-There is, um --

00:03:38.183 --> 00:03:41.487
I think it's so important.

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:43.722
You don't want to get in a
situation where you're always

00:03:43.722 --> 00:03:47.893
saying the sky is falling,
and yet, when Donald Trump

00:03:47.893 --> 00:03:50.563
appointed these new
Supreme Court justices,

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:51.730
a lot of people said

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.165
they're gonna overturn
Roe v. Wade.

00:03:53.165 --> 00:03:55.401
So the sky was falling.

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:58.070
So I know I'm putting you
in a tough position,

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.972
but what do you think --

00:03:59.972 --> 00:04:01.740
It's bad enough
with the abortion ban,

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:05.111
but what do you think
Governor Abbott might do next,

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:07.012
empowered with this ability

00:04:07.012 --> 00:04:09.748
to take these steps
that he's already taken?

00:04:09.748 --> 00:04:11.751
-I saw a headline today.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:14.019
You know, some of his colleagues
in the state legislature

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:17.490
are talking about a law
that would stop Texas women

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.725
from traveling to other states

00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:22.795
to seek their constitutional
right to an abortion.

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:25.331
And this is stuff
that maybe is happening

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.466
because of a failure
of imagination on our part.

00:04:27.466 --> 00:04:29.368
Like, "There's no way
this is going to happen,"

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:30.670
and it is now happening.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.505
"There's no way
it could get worse,"

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:34.641
but it will,
unless we change course.

00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:37.276
The encouraging thing that
I can share with you from Texas

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:39.545
is that the people of Texas
want better.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.214
A majority of us do.

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:43.849
We had a rally on Saturday
in Houston

00:04:43.849 --> 00:04:46.018
for reproductive
health-care rights.

00:04:46.018 --> 00:04:48.287
5,000 people came out
on three days' notice.

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:50.455
It was the largest reproductive
health-care rally

00:04:50.455 --> 00:04:53.025
in the country, and it happened
in the place you'd maybe

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:55.594
least expect it to happen in,
which is Texas.

00:04:55.594 --> 00:04:58.531
But I think that reflects
the majority of us there,

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:00.866
who not only want to make sure
that our rights are protected,

00:05:00.866 --> 00:05:02.701
but they want us to get focused
on the big things

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:04.536
that we can all
actually agree on,

00:05:04.536 --> 00:05:06.738
like the kind of jobs
we want to create,

00:05:06.738 --> 00:05:08.807
focusing on our public schools,

00:05:08.807 --> 00:05:10.776
getting the backs of our
public-school educators,

00:05:10.776 --> 00:05:13.112
expanding Medicaid,
which we haven't done in Texas,

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:15.147
though most of the rest
of the country has,

00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:17.683
so that people are
healthy enough and well enough

00:05:17.683 --> 00:05:19.118
to live to their full potential.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:21.020
Those are the things
that we want to do.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.755
The abortion ban,

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:25.157
this crazed focus
on transgender kids

00:05:25.157 --> 00:05:27.593
and arresting their parents
for child abuse,

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:30.530
permitless carry,
the failure of the power grid --

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:32.698
that's reflective
of current leadership,

00:05:32.698 --> 00:05:34.766
not of the state of Texas.

00:05:34.766 --> 00:05:36.201
My job as a candidate

00:05:36.201 --> 00:05:38.470
is to go out
and meet the people of Texas

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:40.173
to bring them
into this election.

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:42.174
We do that, and I'm confident
we're gonna win in November.

00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:43.776
-Alright. I got
some more questions for you.

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.745
We'll be right back with more
from Beto O'Rourke.

